Template: homelab-roundcube-invite/api_base
Type: string
Default: http://127.0.0.1:3000
Description: Base URL where homelab-api is reachable:
 Written into config.inc.php's $config['invite_sender_api_base'] --
 every call this plugin makes goes through homelab-api's own
 /api/v1/invites/* gateway route, using the Bearer token Roundcube's
 own OAuth login already holds for this session (same field/pattern as
 the existing recipient_blocking plugin's own recipient_blocking_api_base).

Template: homelab-roundcube-invite/ttl_days_hint
Type: string
Default: 14
Description: Invite expiry (days) shown in the invite email's own text:
 Cosmetic only -- the REAL expiry is enforced entirely by homelab-invite
 itself (its own invite_ttl_days config). Keep this in sync with that
 value by hand; a mismatch here would only ever show the wrong number
 in the email body, never actually change how long the link stays valid.
